3.FIND THE CLOSEST NUMBER 
Given a sorted array arr[] of positive integers. The task is to find the closest value in the array to the given number k. 
The array may contain duplicate values.
Note: If the difference with k is the same for two values in the array return the greater value.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public static int findClosest(int[] arr, int k) {
                // code here
                int n=arr.length;
                int low=0;
                int high=arr.length-1;
                while(low<=high){
                    int mid=(low+high)/2;
                    if(arr[mid]==k){
                        return arr[mid];
                    }
                    else if(arr[mid]<k){
                        low=mid+1;
                    }
                    else{
                        high=mid-1;
                    }
                }
                if(low==0){
                    return arr[0];
                }
                if(low==n){
                    return arr[n-1];
                }
                int left=arr[low-1];
                int right=arr[low];
                int diff1=Math.abs(k-left);
                int diff2=Math.abs(k-right);
                if(diff1<diff2){
                    return left;
                }
                else if(diff2<diff1){
                    return right;
                }
                else{
                    return Math.max(left,right);
                }
            }
        }
PROBLEM LINK : https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/problems/find-the-closest-number5513/1


